{% doc %}
  Shared markup of one product-quiz answer card, rendered by `blocks/_finder-quiz-option.liquid`
  and `blocks/_recommendation-quiz-option.liquid`.

  A `<label>` holding a visually hidden, stretched radio (the swatch technique,
  src/scss/global/_component-swatch.scss). ONE markup serves both card styles and both layouts:
  media (an image; with neither image nor icon, a placeholder SVG in the image's slots) → body
  (icons → title → subtitle (inline richtext, links inert like the title's), each only if
  filled). The
  option cannot see its question's settings, so `product-quiz-question-markup` rewrites tokens:
    - `__PQ_RADIO__` (the radio `name`) and `__PQ_CARD_SCHEME__` (the card's scheme class);
    - `__PQ_TITLE_SIZE__` (the title's type preset class, the question's `title_size`);
    - `__PQ_SUBTITLE_COLOR__` (the subtitle's `.color-*` helper suffix, the question's `subtitle_color`);
    - `__PQ_IMG_SIZES__` (the image `sizes`, computed by the question for its image size mode);
    - every part wrapped in `<!--pq-media-->…<!--/pq-media-->` (image, icons, subtitle) is cut out
      when the question's style is Text only, so a text card ships no image request at all.
  Image placement (the question's effective image mode): the option's ONE `image` is written twice
  into the captured string, once per mode, each copy fenced by a mode marker:
    - `<!--pq-fill-->…<!--/pq-fill-->`: the media slot (before the body): the full-bleed image of
      a vertical Fill card, or the left thumbnail of a horizontal card (always this slot);
    - `<!--pq-custom-->…<!--/pq-custom-->`: a vertical Custom card's image in the body's icon
      slot, image first, then the SVG icon. Its own `.media` box (`__custom-image`), NOT in an
      `__icon`.
  Both image boxes carry `.media`, so the theme's loading backdrop shows until the image loads
  (responsive-image toggles `.loading` / `.loaded` on its parent `.media`). They are spans, not
  responsive-image's own `<div>` wrapper: the card is a `<label>`, which takes phrasing content only.
  The question cuts the fence of the mode it is NOT in (Text only cuts `pq-media`, which encloses
  both), so the rendered DOM holds the image once: one `<img>`, one download. Never render the
  option outside a question, the markers would both survive.
  Layout (vertical / horizontal), image size and the selected look come from modifier classes and
  CSS vars on the question's options grid, so generated cards inherit them too: the image takes
  `--product-quiz-image-size` (width; horizontal and Custom) and `--product-quiz-image-ratio`.
  The icon look (`--product-quiz-icon-size`, + `--product-quiz-icon-color` /
  `--product-quiz-icon-bg` when set, and the `--icon-bg` modifier) reaches the SVG icon only.
  The media slot and the icons row are `aria-hidden`: the card is the radio's `<label>`, so an
  image alt (responsive-image always prefers `image.alt`) would leak into the option's name; the
  title and subtitle, outside both, name it.
  Everything the runtime needs travels on the radio as `data-*`: the matching data of the host
  quiz (`matching`), the branching list and the no-preference flag.

  @param {object} block - The option block (its id, settings and shopify_attributes).
  @param {string} matching - `filter` (Finder quiz) or `products` (Recommendation quiz).
  @param {string} title - The card title as inline-richtext HTML (already defaulted by the caller).
    Rendered as HTML in the card; every plain-text use (the radio's `data-label`, which feeds the
    summary, `[token]` values, customer tags and the editor notice, and the image alt) reads
    `title_text` instead: tags stripped, entities decoded so `escape` encodes them once.
  @param {string} [filter_value] - `filter` only: the store-filter value this card selects.
  @param {string} [strong_ids] - `products` only: comma-separated product ids recommended first.
  @param {string} [partial_ids] - `products` only: comma-separated product ids recommended next.
  @param {string} [exclude_ids] - `products` only: comma-separated product ids removed from results.

  @example
  {% render 'product-quiz-option-markup',
    block: block,
    matching: 'filter',
    title: title,
    filter_value: filter_value
  %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  comment
    The whole card is the radio's <label>, so a link inside the title must not act as one:
    `tabindex="-1"` takes it out of the tab order here (server-side, no JS needed) and the SCSS
    sets `pointer-events: none` on it, so a click falls through to the radio. The subtitle is
    inline richtext too and is neutralised the same way; one with no text renders nothing.
  endcomment
  assign title_html = title | replace: '<a ', '<a tabindex="-1" '
  assign subtitle_html = ''
  assign subtitle_text = block.settings.subtitle | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | strip
  if subtitle_text != blank
    assign subtitle_html = block.settings.subtitle | replace: '<a ', '<a tabindex="-1" '
  endif
  assign title_text = title | strip_html | replace: '&nbsp;', ' ' | replace: '&lt;', '<' | replace: '&gt;', '>' | replace: '&quot;', '"' | replace: '&#39;', "'" | replace: '&amp;', '&' | strip

  comment
    The image's own aspect, as a var on the card: under `adapt` (no question ratio) the SCSS
    falls back to it, so the box keeps its height before the image loads. A plain
    `aspect-ratio: auto` would override the img's width/height attribute ratio and collapse it.
  endcomment
  assign has_image = false
  assign card_style = ''
  if block.settings.image != blank
    assign has_image = true
    assign card_style = '--product-quiz-image-natural-ratio: ' | append: block.settings.image.aspect_ratio | append: ';'
  endif
  assign has_icon = false
  if block.settings.icon != blank and block.settings.icon != 'none'
    assign has_icon = true
  endif

  comment
    Onboarding: an option with neither an image nor an icon shows a placeholder SVG where the
    image would be, on the storefront too. It takes the image's two fenced slots, so the
    question's mode places it like a real image (Text only cuts both). An icon is media enough:
    no placeholder then.
  endcomment
  assign has_placeholder = false
  unless has_image or has_icon
    assign has_placeholder = true
  endunless
-%}
<label
  class="product-quiz-card color-__PQ_CARD_SCHEME__"
  data-quiz-option
  {% if card_style != blank %}style="{{ card_style }}"{% endif %}
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <input
    class="product-quiz-card__input"
    type="radio"
    name="__PQ_RADIO__"
    value="{{ block.id }}"
    data-label="{{ title_text | escape }}"
    {% if matching == 'filter' %}
      data-filter-value="{{ filter_value | strip | escape }}"
    {% else %}
      data-strong="{{ strong_ids }}"
      data-partial="{{ partial_ids }}"
      data-exclude="{{ exclude_ids }}"
    {% endif %}
    data-skip-questions="{{ block.settings.skip_questions | escape }}"
    data-no-preference="{{ block.settings.no_preference }}"
    on:change="product-quiz/onOptionChange"
    on:click="product-quiz/onOptionClick"
    on:keydown="product-quiz/onOptionKeydown"
  >
  {%- if has_image -%}
    <!--pq-media--><!--pq-fill-->
    <span class="product-quiz-card__media media" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- render 'responsive-image',
        image: block.settings.image,
        mode: 'liquid',
        with_wrapper: false,
        class: 'product-quiz-card__image',
        sizes: '__PQ_IMG_SIZES__',
        widths: '120, 240, 360, 480, 600, 800, 1000, 1200',
        default_alt: title_text,
        use_zoom: false,
        use_hover: false
      -%}
    </span>
    <!--/pq-fill--><!--/pq-media-->
  {%- elsif has_placeholder -%}
    <!--pq-media--><!--pq-fill-->
    <span class="product-quiz-card__media product-quiz-card__media--placeholder media--placeholder" aria-hidden="true">
      {{- 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder' -}}
    </span>
    <!--/pq-fill--><!--/pq-media-->
  {%- endif -%}
  <span class="product-quiz-card__body">
    {%- comment -%}
      Icon slot: the Custom image (first, a `.media` box sized by the question's `image_width` +
      `image_ratio`, never inside the icon background circle) and the SVG icon in its own
      `__icon`. With an icon, only the image is fenced `pq-custom`; with no icon the whole slot
      is, so a Fill card without an icon gets no empty slot. The fences never nest with
      themselves: the cut in `product-quiz-question-markup` is not nesting-aware.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if has_image or has_icon or has_placeholder -%}
      <!--pq-media-->
      {%- unless has_icon %}<!--pq-custom-->{% endunless -%}
      <span class="product-quiz-card__icons" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- if has_placeholder -%}
          <span class="product-quiz-card__custom-image product-quiz-card__custom-image--placeholder media--placeholder">
            {{- 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder' -}}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if has_image -%}
          {%- if has_icon %}<!--pq-custom-->{% endif -%}
          <span class="product-quiz-card__custom-image media">
            {%- render 'responsive-image',
              image: block.settings.image,
              mode: 'liquid',
              with_wrapper: false,
              class: 'product-quiz-card__image',
              sizes: '__PQ_IMG_SIZES__',
              widths: '120, 240, 360, 480, 600, 800, 1000, 1200',
              default_alt: title_text,
              use_zoom: false,
              use_hover: false
            -%}
          </span>
          {%- if has_icon %}<!--/pq-custom-->{% endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if has_icon -%}
          <span class="product-quiz-card__icon">
            {%- render 'icon', icon: block.settings.icon -%}
          </span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
      {%- unless has_icon %}<!--/pq-custom-->{% endunless -%}
      <!--/pq-media-->
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="product-quiz-card__title __PQ_TITLE_SIZE__">
      {{- title_html -}}
    </span>
    {%- if subtitle_html != blank -%}
      <!--pq-media-->
      <span class="product-quiz-card__subtitle color-__PQ_SUBTITLE_COLOR__">{{ subtitle_html }}</span>
      <!--/pq-media-->
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>
  {%- comment -%}
    Theme editor only: shown (with `data-quiz-editor-hidden` on the card) when no product matches
    this card's Filter value, so the storefront hides it. The full reason rides in `title`.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if request.design_mode and matching == 'filter' -%}
    <span
      class="product-quiz-card__badge"
      title="{{ 'blocks.product_quiz.editor_option_unmatched' | t | escape }}"
      data-quiz-editor-badge
      hidden
    >
      {{- 'blocks.product_quiz.editor_hidden_badge' | t -}}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}
</label>
